A regular ungreased sack has almost all of the protective power that a
greased or oilskin sack has.  The latter are better if you fall in the
water or get sprayed by a fountain, but those are completely
controllable events that won't happen to an experienced player.

The sack will still protect from all the stuff that's out of your
control--burning scrolls, boiling potions, electrified rings, etc.

Sure, the greased or oilskin sack is nicer--but the quoted "there
aren't many uses for an ordinary, ungreased sack" is just silly.  The
regular sack protects your stuff, and it also expands your inventory.
It's an incredibly useful item.


